{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261705501Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: delivery ledger: 2130 hot-path requests sent, 1539 delivered live to the daemon, 591 DEFERRED to the client spool and 0 lost. A deferral is §8.1/§12.2's documented degrade-rather-than-block path (internal/ipc/client.go's Send spools and returns instead of waiting), so the event is durable and the daemon replays it on its next drain — but it is still a sample missing from the top of every gated daemon-side population, so it is counted back in as an over-budget sample rather than dropped\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261730025Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: B-A's p99 CANNOT be certified and its gate is failed on that ground: 526 of the 2064 planned samples never reached the daemon's histogram and are counted as over-budget samples, which puts the full population's nearest-rank p99 at rank 2044 of 2064 — inside the un-delivered block, since only 1538 samples were observed. The p99 field reports the DELIVERED set's own p99 for diagnosis only; it is a lower bound on the real one, never the gated number\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261740223Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: B-B's p99 CANNOT be certified and its gate is failed on that ground: 526 of the 2064 planned samples never reached the daemon's histogram and are counted as over-budget samples, which puts the full population's nearest-rank p99 at rank 2044 of 2064 — inside the un-delivered block, since only 1538 samples were observed. The p99 field reports the DELIVERED set's own p99 for diagnosis only; it is a lower bound on the real one, never the gated number\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261756385Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: hook_ack_rtt is REPORTED, never gated: it is the client-side ACK round trip of 64 in-process observe.tool deliveries, each with a fresh nonce and a real lease, timed through the same ipc.Client a hook uses. Design §7.5 sizes the ACK deadline from it as AckDeadlineMs = L0IngestMs + ceil(slack99), where slack99 = p99(hook_ack_rtt) - p99(B-B) over this same run. The timed samples are preceded by 2 DISCARDED warm-up requests on the same session: without them sample #0 paid a session-registry insertion and a WAL segment create on top of the round trip, and at 64 samples with nearest-rank percentiles p99 IS the maximum sample, so that one sample became the number the deadline was sized from. Its traffic IS real hot-path traffic, so all 66 requests do reach the daemon's l0_ingest and hook_controlled histograms — but this run reads both of those for the gated B-A and B-B rows BEFORE any of the tranche is sent, warm-ups included, so none of it is inside either gated population, and the B-B this row "}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261795445Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"is differenced against contains none of its own deliveries. They are reconciled rather than ignored: a second status read after the tranche counts every one of them, warm-ups included, into the delivery ledger, so a deferral of this tranche's own cannot pass unnoticed. The in-process traffic that does sit inside the gated populations is the warm-up's, disclosed with its own computed proportion. A p99 over 64 samples is still that set's own top sample, which is why §7.5 takes the maximum across three runs rather than trusting one\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261830447Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: daemon-observed hook_controlled_observed (recvTS-reqTS, strict lower bound, no hotPathTailAllowance): p50=2.048ms p99=18.432ms n=1538 — informational cross-check against the gated B-A row above, which adds the tail allowance\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.261920574Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: B-A's gated n=2064 includes 64 in-process warm-up observe.tool requests (Send-time TS, not a spawned process's main() entry) alongside 2000 real hook spawns from the B-A/B-D loop — the warm-up hot-path tranche (warmHotTranche=64, a small, fixed constant) is 3.1% of the gated population for this run; see B-A_spawn_estimate for the wall-clock diagnostic derived purely from real spawns\n"}
{"Time":"2026-09-27T19:15:32.26194929Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/qompack/qompack/test/integration","Test":"TestIntegration_HotPathWarmWithRealResidentState","Output":"          note: B-B's n includes the 64 warm-up hot-path (observe.tool) requests, not just the B-A/B-D measurement loop — the daemon's own l0_ingest count, reported verbatim (conservative for B-B: warm-up payloads run 4KB-256KB, larger than B-A/B-D's fixed representative payload). The other 1936 warm-up requests are admin.ping round trips and never reach l0_ingest at all (FIX ROUND 2, N-1)\n"}
